# plymouth

Plymouth 24.004.60 (Ubuntu's `20250831` git snapshot), the boot splash that draws the distro's theme and the LUKS passphrase prompt, rebuilt for @DISTRO_NAME@ from Ubuntu's `plymouth 24.004.60+git20250831.4a3c171d-0ubuntu10` (main) with one upstream patch, because `plymouthd` crashed booting the live ISO on the Legion laptop on 2026-10-11 (`docs/7 - image-installer.md`, choice 14).

The patch, `debian/patches/script-check-console-viewer.patch`, is upstream commit 88c8dd8d (2026-08-06, "script: check if console_viewer is enabled"): the script plugin's sprite refresh showed or hid each display's console viewer without checking that one exists. A view has no viewer when text rendering is unavailable (the label plugin missing, which the port's package list now prevents with `plymouth-label`) or when `plymouth.prefer-fbcon` is on the kernel command line. Ubuntu's snapshot predates the fix.

The package keeps Ubuntu's source and binary names and the version `24.004.60+git20250831.4a3c171d-0ubuntu10oaxaca1`, the policy's row for third-party software rebuilt from an Ubuntu source package: apt prefers that version over Ubuntu's and drops it for Ubuntu's next upload. Of the nine binaries the source builds, the root filesystem takes `plymouth`, `libplymouth5` and `plymouth-label` (`scripts/rootfs-create.sh`, the `desktop` and `live` profiles), which depend on each other at the exact version. The release publishes all nine anyway (`plymouth-x11`, the renderer that draws a splash in a window on an X desktop, among them): each one depends on `plymouth` at its own exact version, so if only those three were published, installing Ubuntu's build of any other one, such as `plymouth-x11`, would make apt replace the patched `plymouth` with Ubuntu's, or fail.

| Path | What |
|---|---|
| `upstream` | the URL and SHA-256 of Ubuntu's `.dsc`; `scripts/build.sh` downloads the source package into `build/dsc/plymouth/`, unpacks it, and lays this `debian/` over Ubuntu's |
| `debian/changelog.in` | our one entry, put on top of Ubuntu's changelog at build time |
| `debian/patches/series` | the one line appended to Ubuntu's twenty-entry series |
| `debian/patches/script-check-console-viewer.patch` | the upstream commit, with DEP-3 headers naming its origin |
| `debian/libplymouth5.lintian-overrides` | silences lintian's error about Ubuntu's own symbols file (it names symbols with the Ubuntu revision), so the build's `lintian --fail-on error` still gates what this package changes |

No fork of Plymouth: the orig tarball and `debian/` stay Ubuntu's apart from the three files above.
